/-
Formalized the Brockian Framework for the Riemann Hypothesis.
The main result `RH_of_BrockianSystem` establishes that if a Brockian system exists (i.e., a self-adjoint operator B whose spectrum corresponds to the imaginary parts of nontrivial zeta zeros), then the Riemann Hypothesis holds.
The proof `RH_of_BrockianSystem_proved` fills in the arithmetic details:
1. For a zero s, we define t = (s - 1/2)/I.
2. The spectral condition implies t ∈ Spec(B).
3. Since B is self-adjoint, Spec(B) ⊆ ℝ, so t is real.
4. Therefore Re(s) = 1/2.
All components of the Brockian system (D5 action, projectors, Laplacian, potential) are defined and their basic properties established. The construction of a system satisfying `hB_spec` remains an open problem.
-/

